cherrytree-docmodel (1.7.2+docmodel18-1) plucky; urgency=low

  * Export - PDF and HTML now match what the editor shows:
    - PDF: fix large exports producing a file that will not open. A link uri
      with non-ASCII characters made cairo reject the tag at document finish,
      leaving a file with no xref and no trailer while the export still
      reported success. Link uris are trimmed and percent encoded; a still
      invalid tag attribute drops that link only, not the document
    - PDF: scale only the table that overflows rather than the whole document,
      so one wide table no longer shrinks the text, images and codeboxes
      around it
    - PDF: draw tables at the scale they were laid out with, so they no longer
      spill over the line above, and stop reserving a blank line above them
    - PDF: table of contents of linked node names in multi node exports
    - PDF: emit each node destination once, and also when node names are left
      out, so links to it still resolve
    - PDF: render drawing canvases and paragraph justification
    - PDF: export at 100% whatever the editor zoom
    - HTML: style the monospace tag as the character style it is on screen
      instead of as a codebox (no frame, no grey background)
    - HTML: one buffer line is one paragraph; the paragraph margin comes from
      the configured space around lines, removing the blank line between
      every pair of lines
    - HTML: page, codebox and tree colours come from the editor configuration
      instead of a fixed palette
    - HTML: node icons in the index tree
    - HTML: render drawing canvases, keep block elements out of paragraphs
    - HTML: styles4.css becomes styles5.css so the fixes reach existing users
    - Headless exports no longer wait forever on a protected area password
      dialog
  * Undo and document model fixes:
    - Replacing a selection with text of the same length (select "a", type
      "b") could never be undone: the edit was wrongly discarded as a no-op
    - Editing a codebox or table after typing text before it lost its undo
      entry, the model looked the widget up by a stale offset
    - Drawing canvases were lost when undoing a node delete, duplicating a
      node or moving a node, and the loss was persisted on the next save
    - Nodes added by any Import were unknown to the document model until the
      file was reopened, so delete, move, properties and add child on them
      silently did nothing
    - Undo/redo bookkeeping was shared between windows and could skip a
      buffer rebuild in a second window
    - A compound command that fails half way is rolled back instead of
      leaving the model partially applied
  * Password protected areas:
    - Drawings on a protected root stayed visible after locking and were
      saved unencrypted. They are cleared from memory on lock and stored only
      inside the encrypted blob
  * Internal:
    - Undo and redo share one implementation
    - Span merging is bounded to the edited range instead of walking the
      whole node on every keystroke
    - Command stacks trimmed in O(1); node metadata copying consolidated;
      dead command group API removed

 -- Giuseppe Penone <giuspen@gmail.com>  Fri, 11 Sep 2026 22:55:45 +0100

cherrytree-docmodel (1.7.2+docmodel17-1) plucky; urgency=low

  * Password protected areas - new feature:
    - Any node can be made the root of a password protected subtree
    - While locked, the subtree is absent from the tree entirely: not visible,
      not searchable, not exportable
    - Selecting a locked area asks for the password; also asked on document open
      when the restored node is inside one
    - Automatic re-lock after a configurable idle time, 5 minutes by default
    - Several independent areas per document
    - Change the password, remove the protection, or lock every area now with
      Ctrl+Shift+L
  * Encryption:
    - AES-256-CBC with HMAC-SHA256, key from PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 at 600000
      iterations
    - Built on the AES-256 and SHA-256 primitives already bundled with the
      7-Zip sources, so no new dependency
    - The MAC is checked before anything is decrypted, so a wrong password and a
      tampered document fail the same way
    - An unlocked area keeps its derived key, so re-sealing costs about 3 ms
      instead of 670 ms
    - Keys and plaintext are wiped from memory when an area locks
  * Storage:
    - New protected_area table holds the encrypted subtree in the same document
    - The protected root keeps its row so it stays visible, but its own content
      is written empty
    - Descendants own no rows at all while protected, nothing about them is left
      in the file
    - Leftover blobs from a removed protection are detected on load and cleared
      on the next save
    - Save As and Export to XML or MultiFile refuse while any area is locked, and
      ask for confirmation once they are unlocked, so protected content is never
      silently dropped
  * User interface:
    - Tree -> Password Protection submenu, also on the node context menu
    - Password dialogs with a Show Password option, also on the document open
      prompt
    - Shield and keys icons in the tree for locked and unlocked areas
    - Node properties shows the protection state, and names the enclosing area
      for nodes inside one
    - Preferences: idle time before areas lock
    - Search reports when a locked area was skipped; export warns and can be
      cancelled
  * Editing and undo:
    - Locking removes the undo entries that touch the area
    - Moving a node across an area boundary is validated, and confirmed before it
      leaves protection
    - Bookmarks inside an area survive a lock and unlock
    - Deleting a locked area is refused until it is unlocked
  * Fix:
    - New menu entries now appear for users who already have a saved menu layout.
      Previously the saved layout won over the defaults with no migration, so any
      newly added menu item stayed invisible

 -- Giuseppe Penone <giuspen@gmail.com>  Tue, 08 Sep 2026 08:09:17 +0100

cherrytree-docmodel (1.7.2+docmodel16-1) plucky; urgency=low

  * Select tool for editing Bezier curve control points
  * Multi-select, scale tool, and apply properties to selection
  * Separate stroke and fill colors for drawing strokes
  * Arrow and DoubleArrow polygon shapes, closed freehand fill
  * Scrollbars for drawing canvases extending beyond visible page area
  * Font transform matrix for independent X/Y text scaling
  * Fix group scaling of rotated shapes
  * Fix drawing canvas undo/redo scrolling to bottom of page
  * Ensure group drawing operations undo/redo as a single step
  * Allow Ctrl+V to paste drawing canvases outside edit mode
  * Show node ID prefix on all drawing commands in undo/redo list

